  "reason": "Identify ticket sender, location, and devices for office-wide outage report"
}

{
  "hostname": "BL-LT-0103",
  "reason": "Confirm whether the user's laptop has lost connectivity as part of office outage"
}

{
  "summary": "P1 \u2013 Office-wide internet outage reported by Priya Nair (IT Manager, user_id 3, America/New_York). Report: entire office floor lost internet; nobody can work. Checks: account active, no issues. Her laptop BL-LT-0103 shows online in device management with last check-in 2026-10-11T02:53 UTC (may predate outage or reflect a cached/alternate path such as hotspot \u2014 not conclusive). KB-014 escalation criterion met (office network down for several people). No Tier 1 tools cover office network gear (ISP circuit, firewall, core switch, Wi-Fi controllers). Needed: confirm which office/floor, check ISP circuit and edge firewall/router status, check for ISP outage, determine scope (wired vs Wi-Fi, all floors vs one), and provide status updates to Priya.",
  "reason": "P1 office-wide network outage; KB-014 says escalate when office network is down for several people; beyond Tier 1 tools"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Priya, thanks for reporting this. Because it's affecting the whole office, I've sent it to our Tier 2 network team as a top-priority outage. They'll check the office internet connection and network equipment. It will help them if you can tell us which office and floor(s) are affected, whether both wired and Wi-Fi are down, and roughly when it started. Until it's fixed, anyone who urgently needs to work can use a phone hotspot. We'll keep you posted as we learn more.",
  "internal_note": "P1 office-wide internet outage. Checked the user: account active, no problems. Her laptop BL-LT-0103 shows online, last check-in 02:53 UTC. That may be from before the outage or over another connection, so it doesn't tell us much. KB-014's escalation rule applies (office network down for several people), and Tier 1 has no tools for office network gear. Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation id 1) and asked them to check the ISP circuit, firewall/router and switches, and to find out how far the outage reaches. Asked the user for the location, scope and start time.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-014"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
